    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d358">

                <pb facs="0367" n="355" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg355"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/30843: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ford</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-01T18:00:00-04:00">February 1, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. With reference to your despatch 759, December 15,<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d358-f1"/> Iranian Minister here<anchor n="10" xml:id="d358-f2"/>
                    has not approached Department concerning resumption <pb facs="0368" n="356"
                        xml:id="pg356"/> of negotiations for agreement covering presence of American
                    forces in Iran. You may bring this fact to the attention of Iranian officials
                    should inquiry be made.</p>
                <p>The Department believes that the Prime Minister<anchor n="11" xml:id="d358-f3"/>
                    will agree on reflection that in his note of August 21 to the Legation quoted in
                    Legation’s telegram 874, August 23,<anchor n="12" xml:id="d358-f4"/> he did not
                    intend to place the United States in an unfavorable light in a manner entirely
                    unjustified by the facts. Please take this matter up informally and
                    confidentially with the Prime Minister, making the discreet suggestion that in
                    order to put the record straight he may desire to withdraw his note of August
                    21.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
